    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 1st July 2005 erection of an extension to the side of the roof to form a gable incorporating a front roof light, and extension to rear roof slope, was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the volume is below the maximum of 50 cubic metre allowance for additions to the roof, (70 cubic metres in total) for a semi detached house.\r\n"
